      "text": "To solve for \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) where \\(r\\), \\(s\\), and \\(t\\) are the roots of the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can use Vieta's formulas. Vieta's formulas relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots. For a cubic polynomial of the form \\(x^3 + ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n\n1. The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = -a\\),\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = b\\),\n3. The product of the roots \\(rst = -c\\).\n\nFor the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we identify the coefficients as \\(a = -20\\), \\(b = 18\\), and \\(c = -7\\). Using Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\n1. \\(r + s + t = 20\\),\n2. \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\),\n3. \\(rst = 7\\).\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding the product \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\), we get:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + rt + st + rs + st + t^2\n\\]\n\nWe can rearrange and group the terms:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + 2(rs + rt + st) + t^2\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18\n\\]\n\\[\nt^2 = (r+s+t)^2 - 2(rs+rt+st) - r^2 - s^2 - t^2\n\\]\n\nHowever, we don't need to find \\(t^2\\) explicitly. We can directly use the above expressions with the known values:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 2 \\cdot 18 + t^2 = 1 + 20 + 36 + t^2 = 57 + t^2\n\\]\n\nSince \\(t^2 = (r+s+t)^2 - 2(rs+rt+st) - (r^2 + s^2 + t^2)\\) simplifies to \\(t^2 = 100 - 36 - (r^2 + s^2 + t^2)\\), and using \\(r^2 + s^2 = (r+s)^2 - 2rs\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nr^2 + s^2 = 20^2 - 2 \\cdot 18 = 400 - 36 = 364\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nt^2 = 100 - 36 - 364 = 100 - 36 - 364 = -30\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to \\(t^2 = 30\\), but we can directly use the product form \\(1 + r + s + t + 2(rs + rt + st) + t^2 = 57 + t^2 = 57 + 30 = 87\\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{87}\n\\]",
