      "text": "Given the equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\) with roots \\(r, s, t\\), we aim to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\).\n\nFirst, we start by using Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots. For the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), Vieta's formulas give us:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nNext, we expand \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst.\n\\]\n\nWe already know from Vieta's formulas that:\n\\[\nr + s + t = 20,\n\\]\n\\[\nrs + rt + st = 18,\n\\]\n\\[\nrst = 7.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the expanded form, we get:\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7.\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side:\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{46}.\n\\]",
